    "standard": {
        "explanation": "<h3>Understanding Fractions</h3><p>A fraction represents a part of a whole. It has a <strong>Numerator</strong> (top) and a <strong>Denominator</strong> (bottom).</p><h4>Types of Fractions</h4><ul><li><strong>Proper:</strong> Top < Bottom (e.g., 1/2). Normal fraction.</li><li><strong>Improper:</strong> Top > Bottom (e.g., 5/2). More than one whole.</li><li><strong>Mixed Number:</strong> Whole number + Fraction (e.g., 2 1/2).</li></ul><h4>Equivalent Fractions</h4><p>Fractions that look different but have the same value. Example: 1/2 = 2/4 = 50/100.</p>",
